{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Leiden communities (Traag, Waltman and van Eck 2019), maximizing ","type":"text"},{"code":"quality","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each level moves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices from a queue (shuffled by ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to the community of greatest gain, refines","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each community from singletons by merging well-connected vertices at random (a merge of gain","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ΔH ≥ 0 drawn with probability proportional to exp(ΔH \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"randomness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ΔH in units of edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight: m times the modularity gain, or the constant Potts model’s gain), and aggregates the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refined communities into vertices. Iterations start from the last partition and repeat until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one changes nothing (which leaves no vertex that gains by moving alone), or ","type":"text"},{"code":"iterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them have run. Every community is connected: refined communities grow only along edges, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each community is finally split into its connected parts, which never lowers the quality.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Parallel edges add; a self-loop counts in degrees (modularity) or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inside its community, and never moves a vertex.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/communitydetection\/graphprotocols\/graph\/leidencommunities(quality:resolution:randomness:iterations:using:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"